    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14446" root="ربح" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَحٌ</span></b>  <i>A young weaned camel;</i> (S, K:) app. a
dial. var. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَعٌ</span>. (S.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَبَحٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَّاحٌ</span>.]
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>A lamb,</i> or <i>kid:</i> (ISd, TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نصح</span>:) or
<i>the latter:</i> (K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَّاحٌ</span></b> . (IAar, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَّاحٌ</span>, first sentence. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  Also <i>A certain
bird,</i> (S, K,) <i>resembling the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَامِج</span> [which is an
owl employed for catching hawks]: or, accord. to
Kr, the word is ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَبَحٌ</span></b> , and signifies <i>a certain
bird resembling the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَاغ</span>[or <i>rook</i>]. (TA.)

